.Dd $Mdocdate: September 22 2026 $
.Dt FUGUPASS-SCAN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fugupass-scan
.Nd FuguPass QR scan helper
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads frames of one video device, it decodes a QR code of them, and
it writes the decoded mnemonic to the standard output.
.Xr fugupass 1
runs it as a child, with no argument.
.Pp
.Ar device
names the video device.
A run with no argument reads
.Pa /dev/video .
.Nm
takes no option.
.Pp
.Nm
accepts the Standard SeedQR form alone.
That form holds 48 digits in QR numeric mode: the zero-based index of
each of the 12 words of the BIP39 English list, in four decimal
digits.
.Nm
writes those 12 words on one line, with one space between two words
and one line feed at the end.
It writes no other byte to the standard output.
.Pp
A QR code in byte mode is a failure, so
.Nm
reads no Compact SeedQR.
A digit count other than 48 is a failure, so it reads no mnemonic of
24 words.
Four digits above 2047 name no word of the list, and that is a
failure as well.
.Nm
computes no checksum of the words.
.Xr fugupass 1
holds that gate.
.Sh THE CAMERA
.Nm
asks the device for frames of 640 by 480 pixels in the YUYV format,
and it reads one frame at a time with
.Xr read 2 .
.Nm
takes the luminance byte of each pixel as the grey value of it.
It reads frames for 60 seconds, and it then reports and exits.
.Pp
.Xr read 2
on
.Xr video 4
takes no timeout, and it blocks until the device gives a frame.
.Nm
therefore waits for each frame with
.Xr poll 2 ,
and that wait ends at the 60 seconds of the scan.
A device that opens and gives no frame ends the scan at that bound,
and the report names that cause.
.Pp
The stream of the read access of
.Xr video 4
starts at the first
.Xr read 2 ,
and the read filter of that driver starts it as well.
.Xr poll 2
of OpenBSD registers that filter through
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
so the first wait of
.Nm
starts the stream.
.Pp
The
.Va kern.video.record
variable of
.Xr sysctl 2
is 0 on a fresh machine, and the driver then blanks the image data of
every reader.
The superuser must set that variable to 1 before a scan.
.Pp
A plate scan needs a video device on the machine.
A machine with no such device cannot run a ceremony that scans the
plate, and the report of
.Nm
names the device.
A virtual machine needs host device passthrough for the camera.
.Sh THE DECODER
.Nm
decodes each frame with
.Sy quirc ,
by Daniel Beer.
FuguPass holds a copy of that library in its own tree, and it takes
no package of the ports tree for the decode.
.Pa src/quirc/SOURCE.md
of the FuguPass source tree records the copy: the origin, the
release, the license and the digest of each file.
.Pa docs/analysis/qr-library-sources.md
of that tree records the evaluation of each QR library, and the
reason of each pick.
.Pp
.Nm
gives the library one grey byte of each pixel.
The library gives the version, the mode and the payload of each code
that it reads, and the gates above read the mode and the payload.
.Sh THE SANDBOX
.Nm
holds the soft limit and the hard limit of
.Dv RLIMIT_CORE
at zero, before every other act of the program.
It reads the two limits with
.Xr getrlimit 2 ,
and it calls
.Xr setrlimit 2
only when one of them is not zero.
.Xr fugupass 1
holds both limits at zero, and a child of it inherits them.
The execpromises of that process hold no
.Dq proc
promise, so a
.Xr setrlimit 2
call of such a child is a pledge violation.
A crash of
.Nm
writes no core file.
.Pp
.Nm
then opens the device, and it pledges
.Dq stdio video .
.Pp
.Nm
unveils no path.
A child of
.Xr execve 2
cannot unveil, so
.Xr fugupass 1
carries the video devices in its own unveil list.
The promise set of
.Nm
holds no
.Dq rpath ,
so it reads no file of the vault after the pledge call.
.Pp
The 12 words are the master of the vault, so the output of
.Nm
is a secret.
The program clears each buffer of its own before it exits.
The decoder frees the grids and the capstones of one frame without
an erasure, and
.Nm
cannot reach that memory.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/video
.It Pa /dev/video
The video device of a run with no argument.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 after it writes one mnemonic.
It exits 1 on each failure below.
.Bl -bullet
.It
The core limit call of the program fails.
.It
The command line holds more than one argument.
.It
The open of the device fails.
.It
The pledge call fails.
.It
The device captures no video frame of the read access.
.It
The format call of the device fails.
.It
The device gives another pixel format than YUYV.
.It
The frame of the device is outside the bounds of the program.
.It
The buffer of a frame takes no memory.
.It
The wait for a frame fails.
.It
A read of a frame fails, or it gives fewer bytes than one frame.
.It
The device gives no frame in 60 seconds.
.It
No frame of 60 seconds holds a Standard SeedQR.
.It
The write of the words fails.
.El
.Pp
Every report goes to the standard error, and it names the cause.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fugupass 1 ,
.Xr fugupass-qr 1 ,
.Xr getrlimit 2 ,
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr poll 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr sysctl 2 ,
.Xr video 4
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
.Sh CAVEATS
A scan of a drawn code from a camera runs by hand.
The regress tests feed the decoder from the fixtures of
.Pa tests/vectors/seedqr ,
and no test opens a camera.
The probe of the 60 seconds gives the frame loop a pipe that carries
no byte, in place of a device that gives no frame.
That probe reads the report of the loop, and the report names the
device and the cause.
